  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Characterise the first hours (<= 6 h) of the A. oryzae response to hypoxia in an industrial-style stirred-tank bioreactor.",
    "experimental_design": "Fed-batch 4 L bioreactor cultures of WT, the hyphal-dispersion mutant AGΔ-GAGΔ and its ΔaoxA derivative were held at 10% dissolved oxygen (control) or let fall to <=1% (hypoxia), sampled at baseline (B3h) and 0, 1, 3 and 6 h after hypoxia onset.",
    "main_finding": "Hypoxia transiently repressed respiratory complexes I-III and immediately induced complex IV, the alternative oxidase gene and glycolysis, keeping ATP stable; a transient ROS burst was prolonged when aoxA was deleted."
  },
